# Credentials
credentials.json
secrets.py
.env
.env.bak*
.env.*.bak

# Model/data/cache artifacts (trained models, quant_platform.db, output/, logs/,
# and every cache below) now default to living under settings.LOCAL_DATA_ROOT
# (default ~/.stockpy_local) — entirely OUTSIDE this repo, not just gitignored.
# The rules further down that still name these repo-relative paths are kept as
# defense-in-depth only: for anyone on an older checkout that predates this
# change, or for an explicit LOCAL_DATA_ROOT override that (by mistake) points
# back inside a repo checkout. See docs/architecture/data-layer.md's
# `settings.LOCAL_DATA_ROOT` subsection for the full subfolder layout and why.

# Operator-local ticker list (personal, not shared codebase state), plus its
# 3-strike fetch-failure counter (pilots/watchlist_writer.py)
watchlist.txt
watchlist_failures.json

# Python caching
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd

# Virtual Environments
.venv/
env/
venv/

# IDE and OS
.DS_Store
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# Machine-specific build output — scripts/build_macos_app.command bakes the
# absolute repo path into this bundle at build time, so it is never portable
# and never committed. Each developer builds their own.
/InvestYo.app

# Same as above, for scripts/build_pilots_launcher.command's two app bundles.
/Stockpy Pilots.app
/Stockpy Pilots (Stop).app

# Debug output files / DB
*.csv
# Curated, version-controlled data fixtures (exceptions to the blanket *.csv rule).
# delisted_tickers.csv is a hand-maintained survivorship-bias fixture that
# universe_engine.get_delisted_tickers() and tests/test_universe.py depend on —
# without this exception a fresh clone / CI checkout cannot pass that test.
!data/delisted_tickers.csv
# ticker_sectors.csv is the committed symbol->yfinance-sector population map
# consumed by validation/sector_forecast_backtest.py and
# scripts/backtest_sector_configs.py — see forecasting_engine.py's
# sector_configs empirical-derivation pipeline.
!forecasting/data/ticker_sectors.csv
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
# Ad-hoc DB backup/archive snapshots an operator or agent makes by hand before
# a migration/risky change (e.g. quant_platform.db.bak_20260823_082443,
# quant_platform.db.pre-migration-2026-08-13.archived[-shm|-wal]) — these fall
# through the *.db*/*.db-shm/*.db-wal patterns above because the filename
# doesn't end in those exact suffixes. Never committed; same reasoning as the
# live DB files themselves.
*.db.bak_*
*.archived
*.archived-shm
*.archived-wal
*.html
*.json
*.jsonl
!Gravity_Verification_Report.json
# The committed per-sector forecast config artifact, produced offline by
# scripts/backtest_sector_configs.py and loaded (with hardcoded fallback) by
# ForecastingEngine._load_sector_configs(). See validation/sector_config_io.py.
!forecasting/sector_configs.json
# The committed CLI command manifest, produced offline by
# scripts/build_command_manifest.py (subprocess-isolated argparse introspection)
# and read by both scripts/generate_shell_completion.py and
# pilots/commands.py (GET /commands, the Pilots PWA command bar). Committing it
# means a fresh clone gets working autocomplete without running the build step
# first; regenerate after adding/changing a CLI flag.
!cli_introspect/command_manifest.json
# The committed machine-readable settings census, produced by
# scripts/measure_settings_census.py --write alongside its human-readable
# docs/settings_field_census.md twin. Committing it means a later analysis pass
# (liveness classifier, key-partition design) can consume the measured snapshot
# directly instead of re-deriving it; regenerate after any settings.py or
# gui/env_io.py change.
!docs/settings_field_census.json
# The committed per-key settings LIVENESS partition (live_safe /
# restart_required / no_op, plus the capturing site + rule for every
# restart_required field), produced by `scripts/settings_liveness.py --write`.
# Committed rather than recomputed on demand because the runtime-settings work
# consumes it directly; tests/test_settings_liveness.py re-runs the classifier
# and fails CI if this file drifts, so regenerate after any change to
# settings.py or to how any consumer reads a setting.
!docs/settings_liveness.json
# Antigravity's hook config (the .agents/ equivalent of .claude/settings.json's
# `hooks` block, which is exempt from the blanket rule above only because it
# predates it). Must be tracked for the guardrail/verification hooks in
# .agents/hooks/*.sh to actually be registered for any Antigravity session
# working this repo — see docs/AGENT_WORKFLOW_HARDENING_PLAN.md.
!.agents/hooks.json

# Trained ML model artifacts — regenerated by scripts/train_lgbm.py and the
# monthly retraining job; never committed (the tracked ml/registry.yaml records
# the metrics/provenance instead). ml/models/.gitkeep + *.py stay tracked.
ml/models/*.pkl
# Persisted CNN-LSTM/Prophet forecaster artifacts (forecasting/model_persistence.py,
# opt-in via FORECAST_MODEL_PERSISTENCE_ENABLED) — regenerated on the retrain
# cadence, never committed.
ml/models/forecast_cache/
# ML PIT feature-store cache artifacts (regenerated on demand; never committed)
ml/data/cache/

# S&P 500 universe cache — a 7-day-TTL Wikipedia-scrape cache regenerated by
# universe_engine.fetch_and_cache_universe()/_load_or_refresh_cache(). It
# mutates during normal pipeline operation (not just tests), so keeping it
# tracked risks the same merge-corruption failure class as quant_platform.db.
# data/delisted_tickers.csv (the hand-curated survivorship fixture) is
# unaffected and stays tracked.
data/universe_cache.parquet

# Scratch files
scratch_*.py
scratch.py
scratch[0-9]*.py
combined_code.*
pip install*.md

# Generated report output
/output/

# Runtime logs (platform log tail, ad-hoc backfill run logs) — transient,
# never committed.
/logs/

# Coverage.py artifacts
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.json
htmlcov/

# Pilots feature — follow store (local, per-operator runtime state; atomic
# write-then-rename JSON produced by pilots/follows_store.py). Note output/ is
# already blanket-ignored above; this line documents the artifact explicitly.
output/follows.json

# Runtime settings store — per-machine operator overrides layered onto the
# settings singleton at import time by runtime_flags.py. Machine-local state
# that may hold values an operator set live; never committed. As with
# follows.json above, output/ is already blanket-ignored — this documents the
# artifact explicitly.
output/runtime_flags.json

# Runtime settings store — append-only audit trail of every write/delete
# performed by runtime_flags_writer.py (who changed which field, when, and
# whether it applied — never the value itself), plus the timestamped copies a
# damaged store is quarantined to before a fresh one is written. Per-machine
# operator history; never committed. Same blanket-ignored-but-documented-
# explicitly treatment as the store above.
output/runtime_flags_audit.jsonl
output/runtime_flags.json.corrupt.*

# React PWA (webapp/) build + dependency artifacts — Vite/npm regenerate these;
# never committed.
webapp/node_modules
webapp/node_modules/
webapp/dist/
webapp/.vite/
# Vite entry point — a real, committed source file that the blanket `*.html`
# rule (above) would otherwise swallow, breaking `npm run dev`/`build` on a
# fresh checkout. Negation must come after `*.html` (last-match-wins).
!webapp/index.html

# MCP Apps SDK widget build tooling (mcp_widgets/build/) — npm dependency
# artifacts, never committed; the vendored output (mcp_widgets/vendor/) IS
# committed.
mcp_widgets/build/node_modules/
# The build manifest itself IS committed (reproducible builds) — the blanket
# `*.json` rule above would otherwise swallow it. Negation must come after
# `*.json` (last-match-wins), same reasoning as !webapp/index.html above.
!mcp_widgets/build/package.json
!mcp_widgets/build/package-lock.json
# The three widget HTML templates ARE committed source (not generated debug
# output) — the blanket `*.html` rule above would otherwise swallow them too.
!mcp_widgets/templates/*.html

# Real DOM tests for mcp_widgets/templates/_common.js (mcp_widgets/tests/),
# a separate npm project from mcp_widgets/build/ — same npm-artifact/manifest
# split as above: node_modules never committed, package.json/package-lock.json
# always are (negation after `*.json`, last-match-wins).
mcp_widgets/tests/node_modules/
!mcp_widgets/tests/package.json
!mcp_widgets/tests/package-lock.json

# Claude Code transient agent worktrees (scratch, never commit)
.claude/worktrees/

# Antigravity (Gemini) transient agent worktrees (scratch, never commit)
.gemini/worktrees/

# Stray patch-reject artifacts from a failed `git apply`/rebase -- must never be committed.
*.rej
*.orig
